---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ShareRow from '../../components/ShareRow.astro';
import ArticleEndCTA from '../../components/ArticleEndCTA.astro';
import { SITE_URL, ORG_ID, PERSON_ID, SLUGS } from '../../lib/site';

const path = SLUGS.whatsNextAfterSuccess;
const title = "What's Next After Success? The Second-Mountain Question";
const description =
  "You achieved the goal. Now what? Why 'what's next after success' is the hardest question high achievers face — and how to find a goal that's truly yours.";

const canonical = new URL(path, SITE_URL).href;

// Article + FAQPage — schema types preserved from the design, enriched with
// entity @ids so the founder/org graph resolves.
const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${canonical}#article`,
    headline: "What's Next After Success? The Second-Mountain Question",
    author: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
    publisher: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    about: ["what's next after success", 'second mountain', 'meaning after achievement'],
    description:
      'Why high achievers stall after reaching their goals, what the second mountain represents, and how to choose a truer next thing.',
    mainEntityOfPage: `${canonical}#webpage`,
  },
  {
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What comes after you achieve your biggest goal?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Often a strange, quiet drop — you expected to feel finished and instead feel unmoored. The drive that organized your life is gone and nothing has replaced it. This is the second-mountain moment: the first mountain was about achievement and status, often on goals you inherited; the second is about meaning, contribution and becoming who you actually want to be. Choosing that next climb, on your own terms, is the work." } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is the second mountain?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "The second mountain is a metaphor for the pursuit that comes after conventional success. The first mountain is ego, achievement and reputation; the second is meaning, relationships and giving beyond yourself. Many accomplished leaders reach the top of the first mountain, feel empty, and realize the climb that matters most is the one they haven't started." } },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle="What's Next After Success? The Second-Mountain Question"
  ogDescription="The first mountain was someone else's. The second one is the question of your life."
  bodyBg="#EFE8DA"
  schema={schema}
>
  <SiteHeader
    audience="leaders"
    variant="slim"
    logoHref={SLUGS.leaders}
    contextLink={{ label: 'The Legendary Leader →', href: SLUGS.legendaryLeader }}
  />

  <div style="background:#EFE8DA;color:#1B1810;">
    <article>
      <header style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:52px 32px 0;">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:13px;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:22px;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href={SLUGS.leaders} style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">For Leaders</a><span>/</span><span style="color:#C04A26;">What's Next After Success</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,54px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:#1B1810;max-width:18ch;">You reached the goal. Now what?</h1>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;font-size:14px;color:#6E6757;">By <a href={SLUGS.about} style="color:#C04A26;text-decoration:none;">James Carter</a> &middot; Founder, Be Legendary</p>
        <div style="margin-top:28px;background:#F4F0E7;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;border-radius:0 12px 12px 0;padding:24px 26px;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:10px;">The short answer</p>
          <p class="bl-speakable" style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#2E2A22;">The drop you feel after a big win is the <strong style="font-weight:700;">second-mountain moment.</strong> The first mountain was achievement and status — often on goals you inherited. The second is meaning, contribution, and becoming who you actually want to be. What's next isn't another summit like the last one. It's choosing a climb that's finally yours.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:44px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.72;color:#2E2A22;">
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px;">For your whole ascent, the next goal was obvious — the promotion, the round, the exit. Ambition supplied the direction and you supplied the effort. Then you arrived, and for the first time in decades the horizon is blank. Not because you're out of drive, but because the thing that always aimed it is gone.</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px;">Most high achievers do one of two things here. They manufacture a bigger version of the same mountain — more money, another company, a louder win — and feel the same hollow at the top. Or they freeze, mistaking the blankness for decline.</p>
          <p style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:24px;line-height:1.4;color:#1B1810;margin:34px 0;padding-left:22px;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;">The first mountain proves what you can do. The second one asks who you want to become.</p>
          <p>The second mountain is quieter and it's harder to see, because nobody hands it to you — you have to choose it. It's built from meaning, relationships, and contribution beyond yourself. And the way you find it isn't by thinking harder; it's by getting honest about what you actually want now that you've stopped chasing what you were told to.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:52px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="background:#15130E;color:#F4F0E7;border-radius:18px;padding:40px 42px;text-align:center;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#E0744A;margin-bottom:14px;">Find the next climb — free</p>
          <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,36px);line-height:1.1;color:#FBF8F1;max-width:24ch;margin:0 auto 16px;">Stop guessing at what's next. Start uncovering it.</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:rgba(244,240,231,0.78);max-width:48ch;margin:0 auto 28px;">The free Mindset Workouts help you separate the goals you were handed from the ones that are truly yours. Or see where you are on the journey in two minutes.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href={SLUGS.workouts} style="background:#C04A26;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 28px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;">Try a Mindset Workout — free <span>&rarr;</span></a>
            <a href={SLUGS.legendsJourney} style="border:1px solid rgba(244,240,231,0.3);color:#F4F0E7;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 26px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:600;font-size:15.5px;">Find where you are</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0 32px 90px;">
        <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);line-height:1.1;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:28px;">Straight answers</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px;">
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">What is the second mountain?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">A metaphor for the pursuit that comes after conventional success. The first mountain is ego, achievement and reputation; the second is meaning, relationships and giving beyond yourself. Many leaders reach the first summit, feel empty, and realize the climb that matters most hasn't started.</p></div>
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">Should I just start another company?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">Maybe — but not reflexively. If it's the same mountain in new clothes, you'll likely find the same emptiness at the top. Get clear on what you actually want now before you pour years into the next thing.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!-- internal-linking: keep-reading rail -->
      <section style="max-width:860px;margin:8px auto 0;padding:0 32px 76px;">
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C04A26;margin-bottom:16px;">Keep reading</p>
        <div style="display:grid;gap:12px;">
          <a href="/leaders/successful-but-unfulfilled/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Successful but unfulfilled — when the win feels empty</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/leadership-plateau/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Why growth stalls: the leadership plateau</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/who-am-i-without-my-title/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Who am I without my title?</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <ArticleEndCTA maxWidth={820} />
      <ShareRow title={title} maxWidth={820} />
</article>
  </div>

  <SiteFooter audience="leaders" variant="slim" />
</BaseLayout>
